issue.body:
Following "if" statement found on csp_rtable_cidr.c:67 seems to be somehow broken/illogical.

```
if (rtable_inptr == CSP_RTABLE_SIZE)
  rtable_inptr = CSP_RTABLE_SIZE;
```

Since this is the only place where `rtable_inptr` is increased I'm assuming that the idea was to move this check one line above to prevent having this counter overflowing maximum table size.

files.patch:
@@ -81,8 +81,8 @@ static int csp_rtable_set_internal(uint16_t address, uint16_t netmask, csp_iface
 	/* If not, create a new one */
 	if (!entry) {
 		entry = &rtable[rtable_inptr++];
-		if (rtable_inptr > CSP_RTABLE_SIZE) {
-			rtable_inptr = CSP_RTABLE_SIZE;
+		if (rtable_inptr >= CSP_RTABLE_SIZE) {
+			rtable_inptr = CSP_RTABLE_SIZE-1;
 		}
 	}

